Interface composition:
Interface composition means building a larger interface by combining smaller interfaces.
type Reader interface {
    Read() error
}

type Writer interface {
    Write() error
}

type ReadWriter interface {
    Reader
    Writer
}
 - A concrete type satisfies it by implementing both methods:

Why compose interfaces?
 - Suppose a backend service needs to read from and write to a data store. Another component only needs read access.
 - If you define one enormous interface containing every database operation, a read-only component must depend on methods it doesn't use.
